WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.460
kanashimi sasou midnight

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.460
Such a sad midnight,

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:09.400
koboreru ai o choudai

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:09.400
overflowing with love.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.970
kiiroi ringo o kajitteru

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.910
Gnawing at a yellow apple,

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.930
kimi wa hitoshirezu otona ni naru

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.930
you secretly become an adult.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.370
tameiki iro shite mayoikomu

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.370
You sigh, having lost your way

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.140
ai o sagashite ikiteru

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.140
living in a search for love.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.420
suki yo tabun ne dakedo

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.420
Maybe I love you, but—

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.860
akai tsuki ga miteru

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.860
the red moon is watching,

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:45.450
konna ni mo chikaku ni iru no ni

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:45.450
it waits nearby.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.910
kanashimi sasou midnight

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.910
Such a sad midnight.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.980
I can say love

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.710
koboreru ai o choudai

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.710
It overflows with love.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.710
will you love me?

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:57.320
tomadoi no hitomi no oku

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:57.320
Lost within your eyes,

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.270
kokyuu o tomete

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.270
I stop breathing.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.830
kimi no ai o katachi ni

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.830
The shape of your love,

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.480
mayonaka no taiyou

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.480
is like the midnight sun.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:31.860
We've detected a fleet of ships attacking a GP vessel ahead of us.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.020
Distance, 1400.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.360
There's no mistake- it's the warship fleet that we've been hearing about.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:45.750
Don't bother capturing them! Obliterate them all!

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.330
All ships, accelerate to maximum combat speed!

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:57.220
They've abandoned the GP ship and are preparing to withdraw!

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:58.090
Commence attack!

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:08.100
What?! The energy blasts are being reflected back at us!

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.050
Ship 25 has been hit! Serious damage reported!

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:12.290
Cease fire!

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:14.490
The Good Luck Fleet is preparing to jump!

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:15.360
They're escaping!

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.030
Can we make it in time?!

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:19.020
Calculate their projected course immediately!

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:26.130
We're now in safe space. It looks like we've made a clean getaway.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:27.800
Of course we have.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:31.140
We have good luck on our side, after all.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:37.010
But what were those things that reflected our energy blasts back at us?

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:38.480
A new enemy weapon?

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:44.320
KZM ingots that were stored on the destroyed GP ship.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:48.690
The kinds used inside reactor cores and gun turrets?

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:51.830
They must have scattered all over and were just floating out there.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:54.700
So when we tried to use our beam weapons...

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.330
What incredible luck...!

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:57.730
My, my...

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:00.540
They got away without taking even a single hit...

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:05.620
This must be how they felt when they all ran into Seina-kun.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:11.580
Those Who Bear Good Fortune

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.330
Reports of damage caused by mysterious pirate ships in Juraian territory

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:19.470
have been pouring in over the last few months.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:22.700
Moreover, only transport ships carrying valuable goods have been raided,

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:26.040
despite the fact that their routes have all been highly classified!

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.640
We've asked for assistance from the GP,

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:33.110
but they can't even find them, much less capture them!

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:37.350
All we've learned from the Juraian intelligence agency...

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:44.330
...is that it's known as the Good Luck Fleet.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:45.690
The Good Luck Fleet?

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.200
That's the stupidest name I've ever heard.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:54.370
Seto-sama's Mikagami successfully located the fleet several hours ago.

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:56.700
So then the problem has already been resolved?

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:57.670
Don't tell me that they...!

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.310
They managed to escape without so much as a scratch.

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:05.880
What?! But pirates are as good as dead once they encounter a royal ship!

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.980
So it literally is a good luck fleet...

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.720
So you want us to pursue it?

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:16.760
I'm sorry for interrupting your break, but yes.

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:18.230
Understood!

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:21.800
We'll be waiting for good news. Well, goodbye.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:26.370
The bad luck of the GP's Lorelei Seina versus good luck?

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.800
What's hard work again? Who needs perseverance?

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.200
Something about this doesn't sit right with me!

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:33.270
Big Brother.

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:34.010
Eh?

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:38.650
I don't like it when you're so worried!

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:41.620
Your smile is the greatest thing there is!

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:43.820
We would do anything for you...

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:45.990
N- Neige-chan...

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:47.290
Say, something's blinking.

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:49.620
Eh? No way, already?!

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:53.390
Hey. You were moved just now, weren't ya?

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:54.660
Is it the Good Luck Fleet?!

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:57.870
Judging from the mass patterns and energy signatures, there's no mistake!

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:59.030
Already?!

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:00.970
That's our Lorelei Seina, alright!

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:04.310
Never nervous at all, no matter how dangerous the situation gets. Right?

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:05.740
Leave me alone...

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.730
A battle surpassing human comprehension is about to begin!

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:17.720
Raise the spatial camouflage and prepare for combat!

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:18.810
--Roger!--Roger!--Roger!

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:35.040
I laugh too much, don't I?

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:38.770
Well, in any event, my Good Luck Fleet is invincible!

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:42.180
Not even a royal ship could stand up to it!

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:46.650
The mass production of good luck charms is also proceeding well, sir.

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:52.790
Excellent! Transform all Da Ruma pirate ships into Good Luck Ships!

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:54.920
I have some new information to report.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.920
What sort of lucky news might it be?

00:05:56.920 --> 00:06:01.800
Well, the thing is, the Good Luck Fleet's encountered him...

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:04.270
Seina Yamada...

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:07.370
W-what did you say?!

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:12.240
--Here you go. Don't be wasting your time with pointless chitchat.--Ah, thank you.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:18.050
I've been living as a prisoner for quite a while now,

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:20.380
so this is just what I needed.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.180
But who could it be from?

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:26.520
Did Amane, stricken with grief because of my prolonged absence, send it?

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:28.490
Hello there! How're you doing?

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.130
Your mother and I are doing just fine!

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:32.660
What an unexpected surprise!

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:35.160
I'm pleased to see you're in good health, Father!

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:39.270
By the way, when exactly will I be getting out of here...?

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:40.480
Listen to me, Seiryo!

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:46.070
Our company has struck a business deal with the Da Ruma guild!

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.070
Contract

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:51.350
They've asked us to produce all sorts of good luck items for them,

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:54.150
from the tiniest good luck charms all the way to uniforms and pajamas!

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:57.180
And it's all thanks to you becoming a hostage!

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.890
Oh, allow me to congratulate you!

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:02.890
With you supplying the Da Ruma guild with all of its attire,

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:05.490
the Tennan financial group's annual turnover will increase

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:06.630
at least 20 percent!

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:12.620
Yes! Saturating the entire galaxy with our products is no longer a dream!

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:14.540
Which brings me to my point.

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:19.440
I'd like you to stay there and assist the Da Ruma guild in any way possible.

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:21.010
I refuse.

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:22.540
What?!

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:26.680
Father. I am a respected member of the GP.

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:28.850
I cannot collaborate with a bunch of filthy pirates!

00:07:28.850 --> 00:07:32.120
Seiryo. Listen to me.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:37.560
Da Ruma is a client!

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:41.300
A client...

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:43.700
That's right! He's a client!

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:46.530
If he's a client then I have no choice in the matter.

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:47.800
The customer...

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.240
...is a god!

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:50.340
Very well.

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:55.540
I, Seiryo, will put my life on the line and try with the utmost of my ability

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:57.350
to please our customer!

00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:00.050
I'll do it!

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:02.450
A business-savvy man, huh?

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:12.460
That's our Seina-dono!

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:16.730
I knew you would be able to take care of them without any trouble!

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:18.830
No, it wasn't anything that special...

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:21.940
Thanks to you I feel very satisfied and relieved!

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:23.970
I'm glad it's finally over now!

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:26.810
Hey, you! We took time off from our vacation to help you,

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:28.780
and you don't even give us a reward?!

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:33.110
I think we deserve something, like maybe some erotic parties...!

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:35.120
What did you do?!

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:38.350
Are you stupid or something?! I am the captain's assistant, you know!

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:40.350
His achievements are my achievements!

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:42.120
You suck if you won't give us anything for a reward!

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.590
Gimme my erotic parties! Hurry up, I say!

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:46.080
Fuku-chan, go!

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:53.230
Stop! No more claws!

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:57.340
I apologize for his impoliteness!

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:58.910
No, that's quite all right.

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:02.340
Oh, yes! As a reward for this latest mission...

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:04.750
...there's a delightful recreation center near your present location,

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:06.380
so allow me to extend an invitation to you!

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:07.850
With a reservation!

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:08.950
Recreation?!

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:09.550
Invitation?!

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:10.450
Reservation?!

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:12.180
A vacation!

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:15.080
Do they have any erotic parties there?

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:19.390
T-the fleet has been destroyed...!

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:23.300
But most of the crewmembers have safely returned.

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:27.600
It appears we must hurry with the completion of our newest ship.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:30.140
The basic design has been completed.

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:32.770
All that's left is to gather rare objects of good fortune

00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:34.010
and to select the ship's personnel.

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:36.210
Surpass Seina Yamada!

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:39.950
I don't care how many people it takes, just create the ultimate in good luck!

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:42.580
But there's no one in Da Ruma lucky enough to...

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:46.790
Then look among those who aren't pirates!

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:48.520
Where are you taking me?

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:49.920
I don't need to use the restroom.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:51.150
Shut up!

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:53.290
What's wrong?

00:10:00.270 --> 00:10:02.530
T- Tarant...!

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:10.010
This place is not for the likes of you... an idiot caught by a girl!

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.550
Just ignore him!

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:14.350
You look like a filthy rag mop.

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:15.450
What?!

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:17.350
It's a suitable look for a dirty bum such as yourself

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:20.450
who can only attack without warning and pick on weaker people!

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:23.060
It sounds like you want to die!

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:23.790
Stop it!

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:25.490
No! Let them do it!

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:28.390
Understood.

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:40.670
The captain's seat on the ultimate Da Ruma ship...

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:43.140
Which one is the most worthy of it?

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:53.720
W-what?!

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:07.940
See?

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:11.340
A bum who can only attack without warning and pick on weaker people

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:13.770
would have no chance of defeating me.

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:14.710
Did you kill him?

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:18.170
Don't worry. I hit him with the back of the blade.

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:21.410
Which part's the back?!

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:29.360
Enter! That is the path leading to glory!

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:32.350
I'm so cool!

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:02.060
That was quite an entertaining match!

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:05.890
Next is a battle with these three!

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:07.360
What's he mean by battle...?!

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:08.300
You got me...

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:09.520
Who're we up against...?

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.600
Against Seiryo-san?!

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:16.000
Fight him?!

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.770
We don't stand a chance!

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:20.210
Excuse us, but we'd like to quit!

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:21.180
Too bad.

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:22.710
Oh man...!

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:24.350
If we seriously try to fight him...

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:26.250
...he probably won't go easy on us, will he?

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:28.110
That's just how he is...

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:32.190
It's impossible!

00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:34.150
Can't we switch to rock-paper-scissors or something?!

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:38.350
If Seiryo deems it OK, rock-paper-scissors will be acceptable.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:42.160
--Alright!--Rock-paper-scissors!

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:43.060
Better get ready!

00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:44.830
You're goin' down!

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:47.370
Rock...!

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:48.740
Paper...!

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:50.400
Scissors...!

00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:56.440
Alright! We win!

00:12:56.440 --> 00:13:01.380
We win! We win! Take that!

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.120
What a conclusion!

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:05.720
But it looks like this settles it.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:07.650
I take it you all agree?

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:10.760
Money!

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:11.530
Money, money, money!

00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:12.690
So much money!

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:16.300
I have prepared that money for the construction of a Good Luck Ship.

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:18.070
Use it as you see fit.

00:13:18.070 --> 00:13:20.400
Alright! It's hot sake time!

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:24.040
A tiny part of me was hoping you'd win, but I should have known better...

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:27.170
"Party"

00:13:27.170 --> 00:13:29.980
This party's in honor of my appointment as captain!

00:13:29.980 --> 00:13:33.240
Drink up! Eat up!

00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:37.380
Drink until you vomit! Vomit until you drink!

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:39.390
We've got plenty of money!

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:40.550
Here you go, Captain!

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:44.390
Thank you again for choosing me for 1st Officer!

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:51.160
Come on, you know all three of us do everything together!

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:54.660
Hey! Seiryo!

00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:58.970
Hey! Get over here!

00:13:58.970 --> 00:13:59.960
Y-yes, sir...

00:14:00.970 --> 00:14:02.040
What do you need?

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:04.240
Sorry to bug you, but go buy me some cigarettes!

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:07.010
Here! You can keep the change!

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:11.530
"Cigarettes"

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:15.650
Keep the change? Yeah, I'll keep your change!

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:24.300
"Lottery Tickets"

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:30.400
One week of drinking and singing has passed!

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:33.670
You're so generous, Captain!

00:14:33.670 --> 00:14:36.540
Are you sure it's okay to keep this up?

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:40.170
Don't worry! We've got plenty of money here to...

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.120
It's all gone!

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:52.630
What? You want me to be captain?

00:14:52.630 --> 00:14:57.700
Yes! We thought it over and realized you'd make a much better captain!

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:59.800
Please!

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:03.960
I see. When you put it like that, I cannot refuse.

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:09.440
Leave the captain's seat to me, Seiryo Tennan!

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:11.580
We're saved!

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:14.620
So, what about the war funds Da Ruma-sama gave you?

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:16.140
You don't wanna know!

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:21.460
So what am I supposed to do now?

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:23.290
Well, we're not in charge anymore...

00:15:23.290 --> 00:15:25.960
And your family runs a leading financial group!

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:28.360
So couldn't you use just a little bit of your pocket money...?

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:30.830
Please!

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:32.770
Fools!

00:15:32.770 --> 00:15:35.670
All I have in my pocket is this!

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:38.510
A vending machine lottery ticket...?

00:15:38.510 --> 00:15:41.380
What exactly am I supposed to do with this?!

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:45.740
You won the jackpot! You're rich!

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:48.280
--I won.--You won.

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:50.880
You won the jackpot! You're rich!

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:53.350
I was just lying! You're not really the captain!

00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:55.190
Whatever belongs to the captain's subordinates also belongs to the captain!

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:58.060
Alright! Party time!

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:00.960
Don't be stupid! We can't put you guys in charge!

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:02.160
So, now what?

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:03.900
That's obvious.

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:06.100
The ship's construction has now been ensured!

00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:08.530
Next is to collect rare objects that bring good luck!

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:10.030
"Current Good Luck"

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:13.140
The latest mail-order catalogs are nothing to look down upon.

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:16.970
You can order almost anything you want with them.

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:20.910
We've acquired as many possibly-lucky objects

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.620
from the mail-order catalogs as we could find.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:26.790
We're also out of funds. But now we must visit various locations

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:28.880
to collect objects of extraordinarily good fortune!

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:40.500
This is paradise!

00:16:42.340 --> 00:16:46.610
We must find the fangs of Bibagon, the legendary abominable snowman...

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:49.940
Hey! Don't go to sleep! You'll freeze to death!

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:51.810
I said don't go to sleep, you idiots!

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:55.280
Oh no...!

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:59.720
I lost three of my most important subordinates...

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:05.490
I'm... I'm not qualified to be captain...

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:08.630
Thanks. That's enough for my back.

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:10.300
O-okay...

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:15.000
Now you can oil up the front...

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:16.900
My pleasure!

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:20.270
Here I come! Get ready for some oiling!

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:22.640
Look at my face! See, I'm Seina Yamada...!

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:24.680
Get outta here!

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:27.480
Seina. This time I'll...

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:31.150
What is it? What's wrong?

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:32.480
Whoops!

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:35.260
Seina-chan!

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:37.520
Amane-san! Put those away!

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:39.830
What do you mean by those?!

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:40.830
"Current Good Luck"

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:47.700
How many years have passed since you rescued me...

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:50.840
You're so silly, my pink-haired lover!

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:55.940
I know. Being with you has been the happiest time of my life.

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:57.580
But...!

00:17:57.580 --> 00:17:59.680
Darling! Don't leave!

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:03.080
Let go! There are things I must do!

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:05.350
Don't go, Daddy!

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:08.190
Don't say that! This is hard for me too!

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:15.550
Bibagon!

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:19.630
Wha...?!

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:25.230
Is this some sort of show of affection?

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:30.380
I don't think you should have any more, sir...

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:33.210
Isn't that what you want to say, bartender?

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:35.780
I'm a hopeless excuse of a man--

00:18:35.780 --> 00:18:36.680
Hey, you!

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:41.590
How dare yeh try an' swipe my woman's Nose Ring o' Luck?!

00:18:41.590 --> 00:18:42.580
Idiot.

00:18:49.630 --> 00:18:51.700
Ryoko-san's so pretty!

00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:55.240
Which do you prefer, Big Brother? Cooked or sashimi?

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:56.960
Uh, neither if it's a mermaid...

00:18:58.040 --> 00:18:59.710
To think I would wind up like this

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:02.540
right before finding the legendary white elephant!

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:04.340
Please don't boil us!

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:05.850
You three are alive?!

00:19:05.850 --> 00:19:06.480
Captain!

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:07.950
Please save us!

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:09.280
Impossible, isn't it?

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:15.390
Tell me, senora.

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:20.160
Where might I find the valley where the Western Ruby lies?

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:22.330
Wait! All I did was...!

00:19:22.330 --> 00:19:25.230
Keep it down, we're trying to sleep!

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:26.600
You three...?!

00:19:27.570 --> 00:19:30.970
The golden idol! The golden idol!

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:36.080
--Here it comes! Thunder Serve!--Flame Receive!

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:40.350
It would be great if things could stay exactly like this forever...

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:41.310
Yeah...

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:44.690
Not again...

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:48.450
The Pink Opal that's supposedly guarded by... The giant scorpion!

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:53.920
According to rumor, inside this black hole is the legendary...

00:19:54.490 --> 00:19:56.960
My good luck...!

00:19:59.370 --> 00:20:02.170
--Where am I?--My quarters.

00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:05.140
My subordinates picked you up while you were drifting in space.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:06.270
I see.

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:09.040
It was a long journey, wasn't it?

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:15.050
But I haven't acquired any good luck at all! I'm a pathetic...

00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:16.820
What's this vase?

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:19.340
Something I picked up on the battlefield.

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:21.990
The good luck meter...!

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:22.620
What?!

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:23.860
It can't be!

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:27.590
This vase is said to bring the greatest luck of all! It's the Urn of Fortune!

00:20:27.590 --> 00:20:29.460
The what?!

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:31.700
With this, my work is done!

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:33.170
The time has come!

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:42.880
Admirably done, Seiryo Tennan!

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:45.250
Thank you!

00:20:45.250 --> 00:20:47.210
Now Da Ruma can rest at ease!

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:51.510
Let us make quick work of that deplorable Seina Yamada!

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:55.420
You're the pinnacle of dependability!

00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:10.260
OK! Let the ultimate in good luck take flight!

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:16.180
Captain! The engine stopped!

00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:17.380
What?!

00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:20.480
Captain! There's a GP battle fleet off the starboard!

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:21.380
What?!

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:25.020
If the engine doesn't start functioning, we'll be unable to fight or run!

00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:26.720
What?!

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:28.490
We're goners!

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:31.160
Captain! We've spotted a large structure of unknown origin!

00:21:31.160 --> 00:21:34.390
--Recommend we enter attack mode!--No, look closer!

00:21:34.390 --> 00:21:37.000
Could you really attack something that auspicious?

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:40.030
--What do you suppose it is?--Is it a float used during festivals?

00:21:40.030 --> 00:21:41.700
I don't know, but it's worthy of celebration!

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:44.170
--Throw money offerings at it!--Roger!

00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:46.640
The GP fleet is moving away from our ship!

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:48.070
Plus it's left a bunch of small ornaments!

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:49.510
500-yen coins too!

00:21:50.180 --> 00:21:53.540
Unbelievable! It really is a good luck ship!

00:21:55.720 --> 00:21:58.920
Now do you see the true power of the Ultimate Good Luck Ship?!

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:02.720
With this ship, Seina Yamada will be nothing to worry about!

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:10.360
--Um, the engine isn't working...--I am Tennan!

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:27.020
You're the worst, most hopeless, most unlucky boy in all of space...

00:22:32.260 --> 00:22:34.890
Even against your will... (You fail.)

00:22:34.890 --> 00:22:36.700
Even when you're gentle... (You're extremely clumsy.)

00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:41.200
With too much fighting spirit, in vain, it's all coming to nothing...

00:22:41.200 --> 00:22:44.190
You're gonna fail.

00:22:45.370 --> 00:22:48.040
Carefully... (So irritating!)

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:50.040
Or with violence... (Ow! Quit it!)

00:22:50.040 --> 00:23:01.110
You're the worst and most hopeless... you're a lost cause.

00:23:05.560 --> 00:23:10.830
You're the worst and the most hopeless...

00:23:10.830 --> 00:23:15.170
You're an unlucky boy...

00:23:15.170 --> 00:23:20.510
But, any way, I'm with you.

00:23:20.510 --> 00:23:25.670
So, more and more, keep on doing what you do!

00:23:31.270 --> 00:23:32.740
Oh, hello, Tennan-sensei.

00:23:32.740 --> 00:23:35.110
Eh? You've been appointed captain of a Good Luck Ship?

00:23:35.110 --> 00:23:36.750
Really?

00:23:36.750 --> 00:23:39.920
Meanwhile, Amane-san's mother visits the GP again

00:23:39.920 --> 00:23:42.350
and asks Amane-san to do some modeling.

00:23:42.350 --> 00:23:44.220
Next time on Tenchi Muyo GXP!

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:45.520
"Show"
